2) fs_mkdir_p EXISTS
========================================================================

WT L102–135:

    // mkdir every prefix. Existing dirs: fs_mkdir may Err; we continue.
    pub fn fs_mkdir_p(fw: &FsWriteCap, path: String) -> Result[Void, String]
        requires chars_len(path) > 0
    {
        …
        return Ok(void);
    }

- Token: `&FsWriteCap`. Does not mint a cap.
- Walks path chars. Calls `fs_mkdir` on each prefix except `/`.
- Swallows prefix `Err` (`let _ = fs_mkdir(...)`). Existing dirs are expected to Err. Final return is always `Ok(void)`.
- HEAD: function **absent**. WT: **present**.

