3) fs_copy_tree EXISTS
========================================================================

WT L150–169:

    pub fn fs_copy_tree(fr: &FsReadCap, fw: &FsWriteCap, src: String, dst: String) -> Result[Void, String]
        requires chars_len(src) > 0
        requires chars_len(dst) > 0
    {
        if fs_is_dir(fr, src) {
            let mk = fs_mkdir_p(fw, dst);
            …
            let r = fs_copy_tree(fr, fw, src + "/" + name, dst + "/" + name);
            …
        }
        return fs_copy_file(fr, fw, src, dst);
    }

- Dual token: `&FsReadCap` + `&FsWriteCap`.
- Dir: mkdir_p dst, then recurse each `fs_read_dir` name.
- File: `fs_copy_file` (L138) = read then write.
- HEAD: function **absent**. WT: **present**.
- Recursion has no depth cap. Named residual, not a syntax hole.

L137 comment still says `Directories stay a residual (use walk + mkdir_p + copy).` That is leftover wording next to the helper that now does dirs. Not a syntax hole. Did not edit.

